      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Soil pH within the 5.5-7.0 range can impact micronutrient availability for grapevines. In this pH range, iron and manganese are generally highly available for plant uptake, as these essential micronutrients are not chelated by organic matter or precipitated as insoluble compounds. Iron is primarily stored in the soil as ferric iron (Fe3+) and manganese as the oxyhydroxide (MnO(OH)) and hydroxide (Mn(OH)2) species. However, soils within this pH range are less likely to exhibit micronutrient deficiencies due to the relative abundance of these essential micronutrients.",
